# Keep files that are executed on Linux (or sourced by remote deploy scripts)
# checked out with LF endings even on Windows, where core.autocrlf=true would
# otherwise rewrite them to CRLF and break remote bash/systemd/nginx.
#
# A CRLF shebang script fails with errors such as:
#   set: pipefail: invalid option name
#
# Extension-scoped on purpose: a broad `scripts/deploy/**` rule also matched
# binary artifacts (e.g. an exported .csv), which Git then reported as modified
# on every checkout.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.conf    text eol=lf
*.timer   text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers stay CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
